>> title: Pot Roast, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, sunday dinner, braise, one-pot, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: pot-roast
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: yankee pot roast, hot beef commercial, hot beef sandwich, instant pot pot roast, pressure cooker pot roast
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — a roast cannot be judged through a locked lid, so the seventy-five minutes is a commitment made in advance

A whole roast is about twenty minutes a pound. The vegetables get their own four minutes at the end.

>> step: rub, both faces
Rub @beef chuck roast{4%lb}(1.8 kg) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

>> step: sear 12 min, every face
Sear @&(~1)seasoned roast{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~sear{12%min}, turning it onto every face including the ends.

>> step: soften, deglaze the base clean
Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{4%cloves}, @tomato paste{2%Tbs} with @&(~1)seared roast{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and scrape the base until nothing is stuck to it.

>> step: 75 min high pressure, natural release 20 min
Pressure cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1 1/2%cup}(355 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs}, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{15%min}, then ~pressure cook{75%min} on high and ~natural release{20%min}.

>> step: add the vegetables, 4 min, quick release
Add @carrots{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 2-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; halved) to @&(~1)pot roast{}, seal it again for ~pressure cook{4%min} on high, and ~quick release{2%min} at the beep so they stop at done.

>> step: thicken, lid off
Thicken @&(~1)pot{} on sauté with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) for ~thicken{8%min}, lid off, with the roast lifted out and resting under foil.
